<spell-notebook "table-of-contents usage">
	<header level="1">
		Table of contents
		<header>A table of contents lists the page's sections and examples as links, opens the one in view and follows the scroll;  each section folds, and one button opens or folds them all.</>
	</>
	<table-of-contents-tab-bar showing="usage"/>
	<section>
		<html>
			<ui-menu class="ui-docs-section-tabs" appearance="segmented" aria-label="Sections">
				<ui-item link="#using-it">Using it</>
				<ui-item link="#keyboard">Keyboard</>
				<ui-item link="#accessibility">Accessibility</>
			</>
		</>
	</>

	<!-- USAGE:  how to use it (attributes in practice, events, framework snippets), keyboard, accessibility. -->
	<section label="Using it">
		<markdown>
			`<ui-toc>` is a page's "On this page" list:  put it beside the content, and name that content with `for`.

			- `for`:  the id of what it lists;  without it, the page's `<main>`, else `<body>`.
			  A `<ui-tabs>` lists its SHOWN pane, and follows the tabs as they switch.
			- What it lists:  level 2 headings and top-level `<ui-section>`s are sections;
			  the examples with a `heading`, level 3 headings and nested `<ui-section>`s are entries under them.
			- A heading without an `id` gets one (a slug of its text), so every link works.
			- Its links are plain `#id` links:  the browser scrolls, below the page's stuck titles.
			  It lands on the page's hash too, opening the tab and the folds that hide it.
			- It follows the scroll:  the entry in view is lit, its section opens, and it sends `ui-scrolled-to`.
			- Each section folds by its chevron;  the header's one button opens or folds them all.
			  The viewer's folds are kept in this browser:  a section's for its page, the button's for every page.
		</>
		<markdown>
			```html
			<ui-stack direction="horizontal" align="start">
			  <ui-toc for="guide" heading="Guide"></ui-toc>
			  <article id="guide">
			    <h2>Install</h2> ...
			    <h2>Use</h2> ...
			  </article>
			</ui-stack>
			```
		</>
		<markdown>
			```js
			document.querySelector("ui-toc").addEventListener("ui-scrolled-to", (event) => console.log(event.detail.value))
			```
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Keyboard">
		<markdown>
			- Tab moves through the fold buttons and the links, in page order.
			- Enter or Space on a fold button folds or opens its section;  Enter on a link jumps there.
		</>
	</>

	<section label="Accessibility">
		<markdown>
			- The links are one navigation landmark, named "On this page" (its `label` text).
			- Each fold button is named by its section's words, with `aria-expanded` as the fold stands.
			- The toggle's name says what a click does:  "Expand all" or "Collapse all".
			- The entry in view is `selected`:  shown, and announced, as the current one.
		</>
	</>
</spell-notebook>
